The shared libraries installed by zlyme-armhf-runtime are produced by
configs/zlyme_my355_armhf_defconfig with the Buildroot version named in
the runtime manifest. They are not imported from another distribution.

glibc is LGPL-2.1-or-later, with some files GPL-2.0-or-later.
libgcc, libatomic, and libstdc++ are GPL-3.0-or-later WITH
GCC-exception-3.1.
Mesa is MIT, SGI-B-2.0, and Khronos licensed.
libdrm and Expat are MIT licensed.
SPIRV-Tools is Apache-2.0 licensed.
zlib is Zlib licensed.
GL4ES is MIT licensed.
SDL2 is Zlib licensed.
OpenAL Soft is LGPL-2.0-or-later.
FreeType is FTL or GPL-2.0-or-later.
bzip2 uses the bzip2-1.0.6 license.
The PulseAudio client libraries, libsndfile, GLib, and libltdl are
LGPL-2.1-or-later.
libffi is MIT licensed. PCRE2 is BSD-3-Clause.

The corresponding source is the source Buildroot downloads for those
packages and versions. Target LLVM, Clang, and build-only SPIR-V utility
libraries are not included in this runtime. The stage script in this
directory is MIT:

